@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/documentation>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "documentation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The documentation slice of the GMEOW ontology (core tier): GMEOW Documentation Module. It owns — as TBox — the gmeow:doc* projection vocabulary that the self-hosting documentation projection (crates/docs) emits into the gmeow:graph/documentation named graph: the documentation-entry record classes (gmeow:DocumentedTerm / gmeow:DocumentedSlice / gmeow:DocumentedConcern / gmeow:DocumentedMappingSet), the uniform gmeow:DocEvidence justification node and its gmeow:DocEvidenceKind value vocabulary, and the doc-projection predicates. Anatomy, dependencies, and consumer are declared in this manifest; the manifest is the sole source of slice identity and tier."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/documentation> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Documentation Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierCore ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/lang> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/math> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/versions> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "The self-hosting documentation projection (crates/docs — to_gmeow_rdf) that dogfoods the doc model into RDF, so the documentation surface is itself a SPARQL-queryable graph folded into gmeow.gts beside the ontology it describes; the ontology-docs site generator that renders every term / slice / concern / mapping-set page and its proof-carrying evidence panels; and the orphan-zero vocabulary-ownership gate that hard-fails if the projection ever emits a gmeow: term this TBox does not declare."@x-gmeow-english .
